id; no adaptivity gate is imposed. No changed-state hash or \n48-self-report gate exists.\n49:Evaluator-owned baseline constructions sharing main candidate centers: unscaled max-ILR residual; simplex L-infinity; genuinely distinct \n50:Bonferroni per-coordinate quantiles alpha/K; training-only constant ILR center with unit scales; whole simplex. Baselines and controlled method \n51:scores run synchronously with bounded arrays, deadline checks every16 integration contexts,3s/method reservations; no baseline subprocess is \n52-needed and no worker telemetry invented. Candidate methods and required controls have reserved matched allowances before fitting. First method \n53-unfitted+two fitting calls, three prediction methods, nine scoring methods =13 slots at3s plus.1s overhead/slot. Native \n54:terminate.5s+kill/reap.5s+stderr reader.4s <=1.4s, no baseline-worker cleanup;4s episode overhead conservatively covers bookkeeping and cleanup \n55-including reset failure. The monotonic clock starts before numerical dependency imports; deadlines subtract startup120s search/180s final \n56-(smoke20s), reserve15s finalization, globally reserve3s reset+4s overhead per remaining episode across entire list. Conservative joint plan \n57-startup+15+episodes*(3+4+13*3.1) gives986.4s search and2465.4s final, below1200/3600 ceilings. No canonical productive-work floor exists; \n58:measured productive baseline work is recorded excluding imports/reset/cancellation/output. Smoke does not attest production completion.\n59:Scoring per alpha: realized JOINT coverage C, common-probe normalized simplex volume V, U=(1-V)*max(0,1-|C-(1-alpha)|/(1-alpha)). Aggregate \n60-alpha1/3 then seeds1/3 search or1/8 final within case,dimensions1/2 within family,families1/3. Balanced flattened means are equivalent. No \n61-checkpoint/decision levels. Coverage errors are absolute; IID metric uses only LN_IID and DIR_IID equal1/2; shift metric uses DIR_SHIFT. Volume \n62-and control check rate follow full hierarchy. Baseline gap is candidate aggregate utility minus max aggregate of \n63:unscaledILR/simplexLinf/Bonferroni, descriptive only. All missing/failed episode contributions fixed at \n64:utility0,error1,volume1,controls0,correct0, including missing controls/baselines, never omitted/retried/renormalized. Any unavailable baseline \n65-comparison sets entire gap=-1. Runtime is not a scalar objective. Failures retain measured actual duration only in evidence. Smoke missing \n66-unselected shift family emits fixed error1 diagnostic, not a claimed shift experiment; selected case/seed levels use identity aggregation.\n67-Evidence: validated per-case per-alpha method and control outcomes in per-seed solution, merged over repeated seeds with fixed means and actual \n68:total episode duration. Conditional95% Wilson binomial intervals, two feature-defined subgroups; zero-hit volume one-sided95% \n69:bound1-.05**(1/probes) and resolution1/probes; common probes imply contexts are not independent experimental replications. Paired percentile \n70:bootstrap over independent statistical seeds with PCG64 seed62845,20000 replicates for each case/alpha baseline utility and volume difference;54 \n71:predeclared comparisons3baselines*2dimensions*3families*3alphas use Bonferroni simultaneous interval tails .05/(2*54). Overall utility \n72-uncertainty resamples statistical seed blocks keeping all cases together; feature-control paired utility differences have seed-bootstrap \n73-intervals with no sign gate. Bootstrap is finite-seed empirical uncertainty, not an exact distribution-free superiority proof, especially \n74-in3-seed search. Final eight-seed intervals remain limited; unresolved MonteCarlo-scale efficiency differences cannot substantiate superiority. \n75-Publication requires appropriate additional analysis and complete paper; executable metrics alone cannot establish literature novelty, \n76-conditional guarantees or generalization beyond the generators. Final outcomes stay sealed from search and scaffold tuning.\n77-\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
